From e7c6d7c64d051a888bdc220f783d10657bec2f64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thiago Duarte <me@tduarte.co>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:12:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] media: qcom: camss: vfe: Align RDI line stride to 16
 bytes on Milos

The Milos TFE write masters store RDI lines on a 16 byte stride, but
vfe_bpl_align_rdi() falls through to the 8 byte default for CAMSS_MILOS.
For widths whose packed line length is not a multiple of 16 the reported
bytesperline is then too small: a 3104 pixel wide RAW10 frame is
advertised with a stride of 3880 while the hardware writes 3888 bytes per
line. The image comes out sheared, and the hardware writes past the end of
the buffer:

  arm-smmu 15000000.iommu: Unhandled context fault: fsr=0x402,
  iova=0xfd8a5000, fsynr=0x590013, cbfrsynra=0x8a0, cb=10

The modes used so far (4096, 4160 and 4208 pixels wide) happen to have
16 byte aligned line lengths, which is why this went unnoticed.

Tested on a Fairphone (Gen. 6) with a 3104x2336 RAW10 sensor mode: stride
is reported as 3888, a colour bar test pattern is captured without shear
and the IOMMU faults are gone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
index fb7ee2fcb2f1..eb7786a2a0bb 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
@@ -2014,6 +2014,7 @@ static int vfe_bpl_align_rdi(struct vfe_device *vfe)
 	case CAMSS_8550:
 	case CAMSS_8650:
 	case CAMSS_8775P:
+	case CAMSS_MILOS:
 	case CAMSS_X1E80100:
 		ret = 16;
 		break;
